# TenderWriter System Architecture

This diagram illustrates how the various components of the TenderWriter infrastructure interact to provide AI-powered tender management, HybridRAG search, and real-time document editing.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "External / Browser"
        User["User Browser"]
    end

    subgraph "Frontend Layer"
        FE["Frontend (React + Vite)"]
    end

    subgraph "Application Layer"
        BE["Backend (FastAPI)"]
        OO["OnlyOffice Document Server"]
    end

    subgraph "AI & RAG Services"
        Ollama["Ollama (LLM)"]
        Qdrant["Qdrant (Vector DB)"]
        Neo4j["Neo4j (Knowledge Graph)"]
    end

    subgraph "Data & Messaging"
        Postgres[("PostgreSQL")]
        MinIO[("MinIO (S3 Object Storage)")]
        Redis[("Redis (Queue / Cache)")]
        Mailpit["Mailpit (SMTP Test)"]
    end

    %% User Interactions
    User --> FE
    User -- "Editor Iframe" --> OO

    %% Frontend Interactions
    FE -- "REST API (JWT)" --> BE

    %% Backend Dependencies
    BE -- "SQL / State" --> Postgres
    BE -- "Files / Docs" --> MinIO
    BE -- "Async Tasks" --> Redis
    BE -- "SMTP" --> Mailpit

    %% RAG & AI Pipeline
    BE -- "LLM Inference" --> Ollama
    BE -- "Vector Search" --> Qdrant
    BE -- "Graph Queries" --> Neo4j

    %% OnlyOffice Integration
    BE -- "JWT / Config" --> OO
    OO -- "Fetch / Save Files" --> BE
    OO -- "Status Callbacks" --> BE
```

### Component Roles & Iterations

| Component | Responsibility | Interaction Pattern |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Frontend** | User Interface | Fetches/Sends data via Backend; initializes OnlyOffice editor. |
| **Backend** | Business Logic | Orchestrates RAG pipeline, manages document lifecycle, and secures storage. |
| **OnlyOffice** | Document Editing | Loads documents from Backend; sends changes back via callbacks. |
| **PostgreSQL** | Relational Data | Stores tenders, proposals, user accounts, and permissions. |
| **MinIO** | Document Storage | Persistence for uploaded PDFs and generated DOCX proposals. |
| **Qdrant** | Vector Search | Stores and searches document embeddings for context retrieval. |
| **Neo4j** | Knowledge Graph | Manages relationships between entities (clients, categories, requirements). |
| **Ollama** | AI Engine | Runs local LLM models for generating proposal content and analysis. |
| **Redis** | Task Queue | Handles background processing for document ingestion and AI generation. |
| **Mailpit** | Email Testing | Captures outgoing SMTP emails for local development/testing. |
